sh-plugin-gating-hub/releases)[]("},{"id":"p7s3","text":"https://www.dsh.so/artifact/dsh-plugin-hub)"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"**Install (npm, one line)**"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Then restart the dsh service → refresh the page → **Settings → Plugins → Plugin Console**."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"**Three hard guarantees**"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"- 🛡️ **Contract pre-check → rollback point → auto-rollback.** A data-driven **contract pre-check**\nr"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"uns first (message contract / dependency API / config schema / removed API / loader contract);\nthen "},{"id":"p12s3","text":"config backup + a full-tree **rollback point**. A failed install or relaunch **auto-rolls\nthe tree b"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"ack**, a 「roll back to previous」 button restores the last version, and plugins the\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Why DSH Plugin Gating Hub"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"- 🛡️ **Framework upgrade safety, end-to-end** — one-click upgrade: config backup + full-tree\ncheckpo"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"int (rollback point) → online install (service stays up, page never disconnects) →\nversion verificat"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"ion → auto-restart. A failed install **auto-rolls the whole tree back**,\nversion check catches fake "},{"id":"p14s4","text":"success, 15-min hard timeout + stall detection — the framework is\nnever left broken. → details\n- ↩️ "},{"id":"p14s5","text":"**One-click rollback to the previous version** — after an upgrade the framework card keeps\na 「roll b"},{"id":"p14s6","text":"ack to previous」 button: stop service → restore full tree → relaunch → health check,\nstate visible t"},{"id":"p14s7","text":"hroughout.\n- 🚫 **Incompatible plugins auto-disabled** — the **adapt gate** force-disables plugins th"},{"id":"p14s8","text":"e new\nframework cannot load (enable locked; the server rejects `/toggle` with 409 — unbypassable);\n「"},{"id":"p14s9","text":"Check update → Update & adapt」auto-verifies and unlocks them.\n- 🔒 **Plugin upgrade gating** — a vers"},{"id":"p14s10","text":"ion/declaration gate (`dsh.engines.framework` /\n`engines.dsh` + `@deepseek-ai/*` ranges, built-in ze"},{"id":"p14s11","text":"ro-dependency semver engine) decides\nwhether a plugin version may run on this host, so an upgrade ca"},{"id":"p14s12","text":"n't silently take plugins out.\n- 🧩 **Built-in discovery layer** — multi-source plugin market (GitHub"},{"id":"p14s13","text":" / Gitee / custom sources)\nplus the static index of `dsh-plugin` repos (500+ by stars) and a Skills "},{"id":"p14s14","text":"tab (up to 300);\nbrowse, search, one-click install, **zero GitHub API calls** (served via CDN).\n**Ev"},{"id":"p14s15","text":"ery source is swappable** — private intranet npm registry, custom search source (URL template +\nhead"},{"id":"p14s16","text":"ers), self-hosted index source, Git source (incl. local `file://` bare repo) — so an\n**intranet-only"},{"id":"p14s17","text":" / offline** machine can still browse and install.\n- 🤖 **AI Empower** — give the console a package n"},{"id":"p14s18","text":"ame or GitHub repo, the local AI\nreads its docs and drafts a safe, confirmable deployment plan (inst"},{"id":"p14s19","text":"all / config /\nstart / health-check); server components get an automatic control card.\n→ details"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## Framework compatibility"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Measured on isolated instances (fresh `DSH_HOME`, real HTTP probes) — **supported: framework ≥ `0.1."},{"id":"p17s2","text":"5-rc.2`**, no workarounds needed."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"| | 0.1.7-rc.2 (current) | 0.1.5-rc.2 / 0.1.2-rc.1 |"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"| Official plugins page (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-plugin-manager`) | present | **not shipped by t"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"he framework at all** |\n| The official-style **Upgrade safety** entry | shown (hosted in that page's"},{"id":"p19s3","text":" own `plugins.bundle.config` slot) | not shown — there is no page to host it |\n| Classic **Plugins**"},{"id":"p19s4","text":" tab (`settings.plugins.tab`) | shown | **shown** |\n| Server-side features (upgrade / rollback / gat"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"ing / marketplace) | all available | **all available** (every route answered 200 in the matrix) |\n| "},{"id":"p19s6","text":"Errors | none | **none** (the slot registration degrades silently) |"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"So on an older framework the plugin is **the old UI with the full feature set** — the new entry simp"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"ly has nowhere to live. It never white-screens and never throws."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Verification matrix, raw logs and the one framework-side caveat (`0.1.2-rc.1` ships `patchReload: \"l"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"ive\"` for a web tree without the HMR service → boot exits 1 after ~10s; unrelated to this plugin) ar"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"e recorded in `.testdir/fw-old-matrix/report.md`."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Known limitations"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"- Host code changes require a **service restart**; client changes only need a page refresh.\n- On a *"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"*desktop-hosted** instance the console **refuses** to restart and says so: the official path is to\nf"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"ully quit and reopen the client. It never kills or spawns a process there — a manual relaunch would\n"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"fight the host for the port and produce \"The application could not start or stopped unexpectedly\".\n-"},{"id":"p23s5","text":" On a **standalone (web) instance** the restart button is available: it relaunches detached, waits f"},{"id":"p23s6","text":"or\nthe port to free, and lets the old process exit gracefully. The toolbar entry is rendered only wh"},{"id":"p23s7","text":"ere it\ncan work — a desktop-hosted instance does not show it.\n- Live GitHub search depends on GitHub"},{"id":"p23s8","text":" reachability (browser-direct + server fallback;\nduring network-blackout windows retry later);\n- Ver"},{"id":"p23s9","text":"sion detection works for npm-published packages; skill-type repos have no version concept;\n- The sta"},{"id":"p23s10","text":"tic index is capped (500 plugins / 300 skills per build); authors bump their star\ncount or wait for "},{"id":"p23s11","text":"the 6h CI cycle to enter the index;\n- Skills are discovered by `dsh-skill-filesystem` — if the curre"},{"id":"p23s12","text":"nt profile does not enable\nthat plugin, installed skills stay dormant until it is enabled and DSH re"},{"id":"p23s13","text":"le does not enable\nthat plugin, installed skills stay dormant until it is enabled and DSH restarted."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}

